{{also|ljuga}}

==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|ljúga||to lie|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*leuganą}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*lewgʰ-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈljuːa/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|uːa|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|laug|lugu|logið}}

# {{context|ambitransitive|governs the dative|lang=is}} to [[lie]], to tell [[lies]] [about something]
#* Colossians 3:9
#*: '''''Ljúgið''' ekki hver að öðrum, því þér hafið afklæðst hinum gamla manni með gjörðum hans.''
#*:: Do not '''lie''' to each other, since you have taken off your old self with its practices.
#: ''Hún '''lýgur''' alltaf að mér.''
#:: She's always '''lying''' to me.
#: ''Ertu að '''ljúga'''?''
#:: Are you '''lying'''?
#: ''Að '''ljúga''' til nafns.''
#:: To '''lie''' about one's name.
#: ''Hún '''laug''' því að honum að hún væri ógift.''
#:: She '''lied''' to him about being unmarried.
#: ''Ég er á þrettán bíla. — Þú '''lýgur''' því!''
#:: I own thirteen cars. — That's a '''lie'''!
#: ''Hann lýgur því að hann eigi bíl.''
#:: He's '''lying''' about having a car.
# {{context|transitive|governs the accusative|lang=is}} to [[lie]] to someone, to tell [[lies]] to someone
#: ''Stjórnmálamenn hafa [[ljúga fullan|'''logið''' þig fullan]]!''
#:: Politicians have filled you with '''lies'''!
# {{context|transitive|governs the dative|lang=is}} to [[lie]] about something, to tell [[lies]] about something

