==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*leuganą}}. Cognates with Old English {{term/t|ang|lēoġan}} (Modern English {{term|lie|lang=en}}), Old Saxon {{term|liogan|lang=osx}}, Dutch {{term|liegen|lang=nl}}, Old High German {{term|liogan|lang=goh}} (German {{term|lügen|lang=de}}), Gothic {{term|𐌻𐌹𐌿𐌲𐌰𐌽|lang=got}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*lewgʰ-}}. Indo-European cognates include Lithuanian {{term|lūgoti|lang=lt}}.

===Verb===
{{non-verb}}

# to [[lie]], to tell [[lies]]

